            <ArticleTitle>GOTcha: lncRNA-ACOD1 targets metabolism during viral infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/cr.2017.153</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Long-noncoding RNAs (lncRNAs) are emerging as important regulators of cellular processes, but few have been functionally characterized in host-pathogen interactions. A recent report in Science demonstrates a mechanistic role for a novel lncRNA in directly binding an essential metabolic enzyme, glutamic-oxaloacetic transaminase (GOT2); this interaction benefits viral replication via alteration of host metabolism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
